{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And you shall warn them the statutes and the laws</b> — and you shall make known to them the way they shall walk in it, according to the Torah and the commandment. That is, you shall warn them greatly, and you shall teach them the Torah and the commandment. [Jethro] gave him counsel also regarding that which he said, <b>and I made known the statutes of the Elohim and His laws</b>, and in this too there is counsel: to warn them greatly, and to make known to them the commandments and their punishment, since he himself will no longer execute judgment among them. But regarding the judgment that you said, <b>and I judge between a man and his fellow</b> — appoint judges with yourself, for the matter of judgment is too heavy for you more than all the rest, and it is good for you and for them to lighten the burden from upon you, <b>and they shall bear with you</b>. And it is known that there were with Moses officers (shoṭerim) acting as taskmasters over the people, to bring the litigants before him and to press them in the matter of judgment, and many of them were with these judges, and therefore it says in Mishneh Torah (Deuteronomy 1:15) \"and officers for your tribes.\" And there is no need to mention this here, for it was not part of Jethro's counsel."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:10:31.562913662Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}